import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Chapter 106 | Realm Refinement · Sense-Origin Realm · Predatory Faction vs Symbiotic Faction Comparison","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Chapter 106 | Realm Refinement · Sense-Origin Realm · Predatory Faction vs Symbiotic Faction Comparison","no":106,"module":1,"tags":["境界","感元境","掠夺派","共生派","路线对比"],"related":["04-掠夺式修炼体系批判","01-衡元宙核心世界观","14-修炼境界统一划分"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/106_模块1-感元境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md","filePath":"en/106_模块1-感元境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md"}'),n={name:"en/106_模块1-感元境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md"};function r(s,e,l,h,d,c){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="chapter-106-sense-origin-realm-system-comparison-between-the-predatory-faction-and-the-symbiotic-faction" tabindex="-1">Chapter 106 | Sense-Origin Realm: System Comparison Between the Predatory Faction and the Symbiotic Faction <a class="header-anchor" href="#chapter-106-sense-origin-realm-system-comparison-between-the-predatory-faction-and-the-symbiotic-faction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Chapter 106 | Sense-Origin Realm: System Comparison Between the Predatory Faction and the Symbiotic Faction&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module One · Deep Realm Refinement | Grounding documents: Docs 04, 01, 14</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-two-cultivation-logics-two-kinds-of-universe" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Two Cultivation Logics, Two Kinds of Universe <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-two-cultivation-logics-two-kinds-of-universe" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Two Cultivation Logics, Two Kinds of Universe&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Sense-Origin Realm is not only the starting point of cultivation, but also the very first crossroads of worldview: from the very first energy absorption, a cultivator is already standing at the fork—either &quot;I take from the world,&quot; or &quot;I grow with the world.&quot; These two sentences sound close, but they lead to two entirely different universes: the one is a hunting ground where the strong eat the weak; the other is a life-community where all beings rise together.</p><p>This article gives the system-level comparison between the Predatory Cultivation System and the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization.</p><p>The Six Top Axioms are the dividing line itself: the Axiom of Anti-Predation separates &quot;take&quot; from &quot;grow&quot;; the Axiom of Myriad Races Republic separates &quot;my kind alone&quot; from &quot;all races&quot;; the Axiom of Collective Dimensional Ascension separates &quot;I alone ascend&quot; from &quot;we ascend together&quot;; the Axiom of Causal Self-Discipline separates &quot;debt elsewhere&quot; from &quot;I bear my own fruit&quot;; the Axiom of Law Priority separates &quot;rules for my convenience&quot; from &quot;stable and self-consistent law.&quot; The Law of Universal Infinite Equality for All Beings establishes that every being inherently carries Fundamental Infinite Power; the laid-back retain a guaranteed baseline infinity and will not be eliminated by the times, while grinders and peerless youths can stack higher tiers of infinity. Infinite origin is carried by all—the predatory logic&#39;s &quot;only the strong may survive&quot; is already invalid on its face.</p><h2 id="i-system-comparison-master-table" tabindex="-1">I. System Comparison Master Table <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-system-comparison-master-table" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. System Comparison Master Table&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Predatory Faction</th><th>Symbiotic Faction (Anchor)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Energy source</td><td>Devours others&#39; origin</td><td>Takes from the world cycle, feeds back</td></tr><tr><td>Attitude to the weak</td><td>Natural selection, die if weak</td><td>Guardrail for all, not one left behind</td></tr><tr><td>Ceiling logic</td><td>One top over a graveyard</td><td>Whole rises together</td></tr><tr><td>Time horizon</td><td>Drain now, discard later</td><td>Two-way circulation, sustainable</td></tr><tr><td>Risk attitude</td><td>Risk is a filter</td><td>Risk is a problem to manage</td></tr><tr><td>Ethical baseline</td><td>Might makes right</td><td>Causal self-discipline</td></tr><tr><td>Ultimate destination</td><td>The overlord of one star region</td><td>Balanced-Anchor Hyper-Pluralistic Realm</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-the-predatory-faction-s-three-fallacies" tabindex="-1">II. The Predatory Faction&#39;s Three Fallacies <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-predatory-faction-s-three-fallacies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Predatory Faction&#39;s Three Fallacies&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Fallacy of the zero-sum: it believes power is fixed, so to gain it one must take from another—blind to the fact that the world cycle&#39;s energy is renewable and expansive.</li><li>Fallacy of the natural elimination: it believes the weak deserve to be eliminated—blind to the fact that a laid-back baseline infinity lets the slow keep up without being crushed.</li><li>Fallacy of the &quot;enlightened predator&quot;: it believes a kind predator is the best predator—blind to the fact that the structure of predation itself is the disease, not the predator&#39;s temper.</li></ol><h2 id="iii-the-enlightened-predator-and-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">III. The &quot;Enlightened Predator&quot; and Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-enlightened-predator-and-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The &quot;Enlightened Predator&quot; and Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The so-called enlightened predator—that is, the strong who does not kill wantonly, who &quot;shares some&quot; with the weak, who calls himself benevolent—is the most dangerous self-deception of the predatory faction. A kind hunter is still a hunter; his kindness is only the refinement of his prey-management. History repeatedly shows that the &quot;enlightened&quot; era of a predatory system is always the eve of regression: once the hunting grounds are exhausted, the &quot;benevolent&quot; strong are the first to turn on their own people.</p><h2 id="iv-the-righteous-rogue-a-warning-to-the-chosen" tabindex="-1">IV. The Righteous Rogue: A Warning to the &quot;Chosen&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-righteous-rogue-a-warning-to-the-chosen" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Righteous Rogue: A Warning to the &quot;Chosen&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Symbiotic faction does not pretend that its own side is perfect. The most insidious variant is the &quot;righteous rogue&quot;: one who uses the mantle of justice to still plunder, who says &quot;I do this for the symbiosis&quot; while draining others for his own breakthrough.</p><p>Take Lin Hao, the protagonist of this universe, as the touchstone: his path is not to become the strongest in a hunting ground, but to prove that the strong can rise while still leaving the weak a way home. Whenever he is tempted to say &quot;I am special, so the rules don&#39;t apply to me,&quot; that is the precise moment the Shortcut Inner Demon knocks—this is the inner line every cultivator of the symbiotic faction must hold.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-landing-points" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Landing Points <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-landing-points" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Landing Points&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Anti-energy-tier waste: the predatory faction&#39;s &quot;strong eat weak&quot; wastes more evolutionary potential than any war; the symbiotic faction&#39;s two-way circulation is the true high-efficiency.</li><li>Anti-predation: every row of the master table is a red line the symbiotic faction will not cross.</li><li>Tang-Luo ceiling comparison: the predatory faction&#39;s ceiling is one overlord over a graveyard; the symbiotic faction&#39;s ceiling lifts the whole cosmos up.</li><li>Full Myriad-Race coverage: the master table covers every dimension from energy source to final destination, leaving no blind spot.</li><li>Hyper-pluralistic full openness: the comparison itself is open evidence—the predatory faction dares not publish it, because every dimension exposes its own smallness.</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A table does not need rhetoric; the two columns already speak. In the Sense-Origin Realm, the first absorption a cultivator chooses decides which column he will stand in for the rest of his life—this is why this comparison is placed at the very beginning of the whole library: let every reader see, before choosing the path, which universe he is about to enter.</p><h2 id="links" tabindex="-1">Links <a class="header-anchor" href="#links" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Links&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-掠夺式修炼体系批判">04-Critique of the Predatory Cultivation System</a> · <a href="./01-衡元宙核心世界观">01-Core Worldview of Heng Yuan Zhou</a> · <a href="./14-修炼境界统一划分">14-Unified Classification of Cultivation Realms</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',21)])])}const f=t(n,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,f as default};
